    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d227-a5">

                <pb facs="0463" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg415"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 395.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Crosby to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >War Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington
                                City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1877-06-15"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 15,
                    1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit, for your
                    information, a copy of a telegram from Lieutenant-General Sheridan dated the
                    15th instant, reporting that Colonel Shafter has interned a number of Mexican
                    soldiers recently engaged in conflicts on the Rio Grande, and who fled to our
                    side of the river; also a copy of the reply of the Adjutant-General of the Army
                    to General Sheridan’s question as to what disposition should be made of the
                    persons above referred to.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>H. T. CROSBY,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Chief
                    Clerk.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
